WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:41.736 --> 00:00:42.396
In Vietnam,

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:45.539
They say that a smile makes you look 10 years younger.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.441
In this country marked by so much...

00:00:49.441 --> 00:00:50.021
So many tragedies,

00:00:50.301 --> 00:00:51.042
so many wars,

00:00:51.302 --> 00:00:54.404
and today, due to increasingly frequent natural disasters,

00:00:54.944 --> 00:00:56.645
if everyone looks ten years younger,

00:00:57.245 --> 00:00:57.746
that's because here,

00:00:58.306 --> 00:00:59.026
Whatever happens,

00:00:59.487 --> 00:01:00.888
Happiness is essential.

00:01:26.084 --> 00:01:26.484
To struggle against,

00:01:26.884 --> 00:01:27.424
fight,

00:01:27.724 --> 00:01:28.605
not to complain,

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:29.564
react,

00:01:29.926 --> 00:01:30.486
survive,

00:01:30.865 --> 00:01:31.847
to force destiny,

00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:33.227
to overcome the elements

00:01:33.707 --> 00:01:47.754
These are the watchwords of an entire population that displays unfailing energy in the face of the wrath of the monsoon, which from spring onwards plunges the center of the country into expected but increasingly virulent turmoil year after year.

00:01:55.956 --> 00:01:58.096
Originally from Guangbin province,

00:01:58.516 --> 00:02:03.599
A woman decided to fight against the fury of the elements and their dramatic consequences.

00:02:04.019 --> 00:02:04.661
Her name is

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:05.381
Link.

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:14.365
Ever since I was very little,

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:15.687
I have always loved nature.

00:02:16.146 --> 00:02:18.448
That's why I decided to study agronomy.

00:02:19.149 --> 00:02:19.668
And now,

00:02:20.429 --> 00:02:23.191
I am lucky with my job to truly do what I love.

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:37.759
I work for a government organization committed to environmental protection and which aims to safeguard natural resources as best as possible.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:44.183
The organization has a presence all over the world, and particularly here.

00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:45.103
in Vietnam.

00:02:47.885 --> 00:02:51.268
My goal in my work is not only to protect the environment,

00:02:51.828 --> 00:02:54.748
but above all, to seek to help people in difficulty,

00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:57.810
by trying to improve their living conditions.

00:03:08.503 --> 00:03:09.164
In Vietnam,

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:10.606
Water is everywhere.

00:03:11.026 --> 00:03:11.787
source of life.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.550
One should not be fooled by its apparent tranquility.

00:03:16.475 --> 00:03:17.938
With global warming,

00:03:18.237 --> 00:03:23.263
The monsoon becomes less predictable and its effects are amplified by an unleashing of the elements.

00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:25.545
The village loudspeakers,

00:03:25.746 --> 00:03:29.650
Radio and especially television allow residents to be informed.

00:03:30.211 --> 00:03:35.436
The Dong Hoi broadcasting center regularly experiences the effects of the monsoon.

00:03:41.876 --> 00:03:42.477
Flood,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.258
destruction of the forest,

00:03:44.638 --> 00:03:45.199
erosion,

00:03:45.639 --> 00:03:47.099
The sand is invading the shores,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.102
The earth changes its contours.

00:03:49.502 --> 00:03:51.764
The water is rising, yet drought looms.

00:03:52.324 --> 00:03:55.987
But the energy of the Vietnamese is there to counter the effects of nature.

00:04:04.144 --> 00:04:08.606
These news images are a valuable source of information for Lien.

00:04:08.966 --> 00:04:10.228
Because after the disasters,

00:04:10.608 --> 00:04:13.370
Her job is to realize this for herself.

00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:14.031
on the ground,

00:04:14.471 --> 00:04:15.752
actions to be taken.

00:04:17.733 --> 00:04:18.694
I must admit that...

00:04:18.973 --> 00:04:20.935
What is difficult in my daily work,

00:04:21.635 --> 00:04:24.677
It's about feeling alone and helpless in the face of difficulties.

00:04:26.459 --> 00:04:26.899
Fortunately,

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:27.980
with my colleagues,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.901
We share the same beliefs.

00:04:30.942 --> 00:04:31.483
Together,

00:04:31.863 --> 00:04:40.649
We seek to spread the idea that we must do everything possible to protect natural resources and that we must find solutions to improve people's living conditions.

00:04:48.774 --> 00:04:48.894
Oh,

00:04:49.094 --> 00:04:49.795
Good morning !

00:04:51.336 --> 00:04:52.136
How did it go?

00:04:52.216 --> 00:04:53.257
The last flood?

00:04:54.338 --> 00:04:55.178
It's already been two months.

00:04:55.218 --> 00:04:56.459
The water rose all the way to the roof.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.600
At the level of the roof of the house?

00:04:58.941 --> 00:04:59.061
Yes,

00:04:59.101 --> 00:04:59.221
Yes,

00:04:59.521 --> 00:05:01.382
up to the roof.

00:05:01.383 --> 00:05:02.843
And what did you do when the water arrived?

00:05:04.044 --> 00:05:04.544
Fortunately,

00:05:04.705 --> 00:05:06.546
There was a rescue team that evacuated us.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.088
We're here today to see what we can do for you.

00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:12.330
Has anyone come by to help you since then?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.030
Yes,

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:14.251
the local manager.

00:05:14.311 --> 00:05:29.556
From the village, this woman has lost everything; her house has already collapsed several times in recent years, swept away by tornadoes. Each time, she rebuilt it until the day she made a big decision last year with

00:05:29.596 --> 00:05:40.279
With all her savings, she bought several tons of cement to build a solid house before the rainy season, but she was ignoring climate change, because against all odds

00:05:40.643 --> 00:05:46.345
Rains from Ille-le-Vienne suddenly fell on the village with the announcement of spring and all the cement was lost.

00:05:46.965 --> 00:05:48.526
All my brothers and sisters rushed over.

00:05:49.146 --> 00:05:50.546
There are those who brought me rice,

00:05:50.967 --> 00:05:52.087
others, drinking water,

00:05:52.847 --> 00:05:55.328
because we no longer had any possibility of obtaining drinking water.

00:05:56.969 --> 00:06:03.371
The Ienne and the women of the Women Union association are seeking to find a solution so that she finally has a solid roof over her head.

00:06:06.063 --> 00:06:07.324
Kuang Bin province,

00:06:07.544 --> 00:06:08.524
in the center of the country,

00:06:08.925 --> 00:06:12.627
has been hit by more than thirty typhoons in the last 50 years.

00:06:13.007 --> 00:06:19.631
And we are seeing that floods are now much more violent than those that occurred during the first half of the last century.

00:06:22.253 --> 00:06:22.853
There you see,

00:06:23.293 --> 00:06:25.715
These are images from last year's flood.

00:06:26.275 --> 00:06:27.315
in October 2007.

00:06:28.756 --> 00:06:28.956
We,

00:06:29.016 --> 00:06:29.857
journalists,

00:06:30.017 --> 00:06:32.759
We went there immediately to do an on-site report.

00:06:36.313 --> 00:06:39.676
The water rose up to the roof and there were things floating everywhere.

00:06:40.857 --> 00:06:41.638
Everything was destroyed.

00:06:43.019 --> 00:06:43.479
Right after that,

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.241
The military arrived to intervene.

00:06:47.863 --> 00:06:47.983
There,

00:06:48.103 --> 00:06:48.484
You see,

00:06:48.984 --> 00:06:50.225
to access the flooded areas,

00:06:50.606 --> 00:06:51.887
We take the rescue boats.

00:06:52.447 --> 00:06:54.228
Because they are the only ones capable of going against the current.

00:06:55.409 --> 00:06:57.490
The small boats belonging to the locals are not powerful enough.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.071
They risk being swept away by the force of the current.

00:07:02.552 --> 00:07:02.992
Today,

00:07:03.433 --> 00:07:06.494
The effects of the monsoon have become impossible to predict.

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:09.556
And the peaks of the phenomenon are becoming increasingly difficult to imagine.

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:14.438
Causing floods and landslides that have affected many victims.

00:07:19.751 --> 00:07:22.333
While the effects of the monsoon are unpredictable,

00:07:22.694 --> 00:07:23.334
the scenario,

00:07:23.454 --> 00:07:23.615
him,

00:07:24.035 --> 00:07:24.896
is always the same.

00:07:25.316 --> 00:07:27.037
It all starts at the weather center.

00:07:27.938 --> 00:07:30.100
The figures for the instruments speak for themselves.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.101
Depression,

00:07:31.641 --> 00:07:32.742
wind acceleration,

00:07:33.083 --> 00:07:34.444
cloudy disturbances,

00:07:34.744 --> 00:07:38.748
formation of pockets of warm air in opposition to masses of cold air.

00:07:39.268 --> 00:07:40.029
Six months a year,

00:07:40.369 --> 00:07:42.611
Vietnam is under close surveillance.

00:07:45.877 --> 00:07:49.621
It's fortunate that the government is concerned about at-risk regions that are isolated.

00:07:50.863 --> 00:07:57.090
That's why we've set up a radio communication system for remote areas that don't get television reception.

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:00.454
Just before the floods,

00:08:00.815 --> 00:08:03.919
Residents are warned by radio depending on the level of danger.

00:08:04.775 --> 00:08:05.476
For example,

00:08:06.016 --> 00:08:07.497
if a disaster is looming,

00:08:07.797 --> 00:08:11.559
They issue alerts every hour, and even every half hour if necessary.

00:08:16.082 --> 00:08:17.943
To mobilize against the floods,

00:08:19.344 --> 00:08:23.967
Consider regrouping urgently and organizing the protection of people and property.

00:08:24.647 --> 00:08:25.968
This is an exercise.

00:08:26.609 --> 00:08:28.130
This is an alert exercise.

00:08:31.779 --> 00:08:32.660
In case of an alert,

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.422
even with resources that may seem paltry,

00:08:35.642 --> 00:08:39.024
Everyone is mobilizing to fight against a possible rise in water levels.

00:08:40.646 --> 00:08:41.746
When there is a flood,

00:08:41.807 --> 00:08:44.228
Does the manager summon you directly to the location each time?

00:08:44.809 --> 00:08:44.929
Yes,

00:08:44.969 --> 00:08:45.209
That's it.

00:08:45.589 --> 00:08:46.470
Do people come in groups?

00:08:47.371 --> 00:08:47.511
Yes,

00:08:47.531 --> 00:08:48.792
in groups or individually.

00:08:48.972 --> 00:08:50.793
All the residents come to lend a hand.

00:08:58.916 --> 00:09:00.997
When a storm or cyclone is approaching,

00:09:01.237 --> 00:09:07.041
We only have a few hours to prepare and find the right ways to protect ourselves against the floods.

00:09:08.362 --> 00:09:08.882
Normally,

00:09:09.743 --> 00:09:10.604
the water remains at that level,

00:09:11.764 --> 00:09:12.145
but...

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:13.925
As soon as it starts to rain,

00:09:14.565 --> 00:09:16.486
It's rising very, very quickly.

00:09:16.826 --> 00:09:17.546
How high does it go?

00:09:18.406 --> 00:09:19.826
The water can rise above the roofs of the houses.

00:09:20.166 --> 00:09:21.187
those that can be seen over there.

00:09:22.587 --> 00:09:24.727
And the water flows down to these rice paddies,

00:09:25.648 --> 00:09:26.968
So, what about those opposite us?

00:09:27.828 --> 00:09:27.948
Yes,

00:09:28.008 --> 00:09:28.728
all the way to the rice paddies,

00:09:28.748 --> 00:09:30.869
all the way to the field that could be seen at the foot of the mountains.

00:09:33.889 --> 00:09:35.570
A small, newly dug canal,

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:42.211
A simple dam of leaves will contain the current and divert the water below the rice paddies.

00:09:48.759 --> 00:09:52.483
Lien knows all the methods the villagers use to protect themselves.

00:09:52.824 --> 00:09:57.169
Each time, she is equally impressed by the energy he puts into facing the elements.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.440
In general,

00:10:17.021 --> 00:10:17.842
after the flood,

00:10:18.502 --> 00:10:19.544
There are landslides.

00:10:20.505 --> 00:10:25.530
The trees are being uprooted, and so people are finding themselves in a truly catastrophic situation.

00:10:27.715 --> 00:10:29.116
And by the time the water recedes,

00:10:30.057 --> 00:10:31.838
It takes at least 5 to 7 days.

00:10:33.579 --> 00:10:35.320
Several rescuers told me that sometimes,

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.161
They arrive too late to intervene.

00:10:38.221 --> 00:10:39.682
When people disappear,

00:10:40.042 --> 00:10:41.343
The rescuers are taking it very badly.

00:10:42.404 --> 00:10:44.505
There are people who try to help others,

00:10:44.885 --> 00:10:48.367
but who consequently put themselves in danger to the point that some disappear in turn.

00:11:12.935 --> 00:11:14.137
Just after this flood,

00:11:14.858 --> 00:11:16.900
Not only did people in the region mobilize,

00:11:17.461 --> 00:11:18.643
but also all the people of the country.

00:11:19.384 --> 00:11:20.826
They sent food,

00:11:21.146 --> 00:11:21.907
They supported them.

00:11:21.927 --> 00:11:22.267
You see.

00:11:23.569 --> 00:11:25.131
Aid has arrived from absolutely everywhere.

00:11:31.759 --> 00:11:34.501
A testament to this solidarity so prevalent in Vietnam,

00:11:35.062 --> 00:11:39.986
The IEN is working to raise awareness among remote populations about the risk of flooding.

00:11:40.687 --> 00:11:43.209
In particular, children from the poorest families,

00:11:43.569 --> 00:11:48.353
those who live on small boats and are the first to be exposed to the danger of the monsoon.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.001
Lien's message is clear.

00:12:16.281 --> 00:12:26.546
It is absolutely essential that children get into the habit of wearing life jackets to protect themselves from drowning, even when going to school as soon as the weather presents risks.

00:12:41.939 --> 00:12:45.002
When she participates in the distribution of life jackets,

00:12:45.303 --> 00:12:47.085
She can't help but think that,

00:12:47.605 --> 00:12:48.766
amidst the general good cheer,

00:12:49.127 --> 00:12:50.969
A deep distress is hidden beneath the surface.

00:12:51.369 --> 00:12:54.152
that of the memory of the parents of some of her children,

00:12:54.593 --> 00:12:56.715
disappeared during the last flood.

00:13:32.709 --> 00:13:39.596
Môn giã căng căng đời tựa Ta mê lây chung vui

00:13:40.857 --> 00:13:46.062
Còng phân chia lòng nói tiếng cười

00:13:46.663 --> 00:13:50.146
Cùng nắm tay ta kia kinh sanh nơi

00:13:50.687 --> 00:13:52.849
Nào cho nhau những gì

00:14:01.029 --> 00:14:02.350
In the Guangbin region,

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.411
Many animals have died.

00:14:05.172 --> 00:14:08.554
I went there and realized what it represented.

00:14:08.594 --> 00:14:11.856
this loss of livestock is a problem for families who are very poor.

00:14:14.098 --> 00:14:15.158
During the disaster,

00:14:15.518 --> 00:14:17.539
People no longer care about what they own.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:18.860
But afterwards,

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:22.221
They realize the economic loss this represents for them.

00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:23.522
That's huge.

00:14:24.322 --> 00:14:27.224
I was really very touched and I feel very unhappy for them.

00:14:29.525 --> 00:14:30.805
Even when you've lost everything,

00:14:31.286 --> 00:14:33.387
We keep smiling.

00:14:33.388 --> 00:14:34.227
We couldn't do anything.

00:14:38.069 --> 00:14:38.749
I've lost everything.

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:40.410
The house,

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:41.931
the furniture.

00:14:42.595 --> 00:14:43.216
The harvests,

00:14:44.096 --> 00:14:44.857
Absolutely everything.

00:14:45.938 --> 00:14:47.419
We can no longer adapt to the climate.

00:14:47.999 --> 00:14:48.680
like in the old days.

00:14:51.582 --> 00:14:52.363
That's how it is now.

00:14:53.284 --> 00:14:53.744
That's how it is.

00:14:56.206 --> 00:14:57.147
When you've lost everything,

00:14:57.567 --> 00:14:58.728
We keep smiling.

00:14:58.989 --> 00:15:00.250
even when the dikes,

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:03.232
built to retain rainwater and water from streams,

00:15:03.712 --> 00:15:04.533
do not resist,

00:15:04.753 --> 00:15:06.975
with dramatic consequences for people,

00:15:07.436 --> 00:15:07.956
housing,

00:15:08.316 --> 00:15:10.318
crops and infrastructure.

00:15:49.675 --> 00:15:50.556
It went up to this point.

00:15:50.956 --> 00:15:53.277
This is truly the biggest flood I've ever seen.

00:15:59.581 --> 00:15:59.961
But you know,

00:16:00.001 --> 00:16:00.481
This year,

00:16:00.642 --> 00:16:03.463
I'm really afraid it will be even worse than last year's.

00:16:04.184 --> 00:16:06.585
Even though last year's was already incredible.

00:16:11.887 --> 00:16:12.848
It covered everything.

00:16:12.868 --> 00:16:13.288
the road,

00:16:13.328 --> 00:16:13.848
the trees,

00:16:13.888 --> 00:16:14.629
Everything was underwater.

00:16:14.849 --> 00:16:16.170
There were tree trunks everywhere,

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.231
It even rose right up to the electric fence.

00:16:18.371 --> 00:16:20.192
practically at rooftop level.

00:16:25.676 --> 00:16:28.558
The state will have to consider rebuilding the bridge because now,

00:16:28.958 --> 00:16:29.959
when the cars come barreling down the road,

00:16:30.659 --> 00:16:31.540
Accidents happen.

00:16:43.736 --> 00:16:47.098
Because there are people who live in very remote forested areas,

00:16:47.839 --> 00:16:48.499
in my work,

00:16:48.579 --> 00:16:51.201
Access conditions are sometimes very difficult.

00:16:52.122 --> 00:16:52.742
For example,

00:16:53.162 --> 00:16:55.004
There are roads inaccessible by car.

00:16:55.464 --> 00:16:55.844
Sometimes,

00:16:55.884 --> 00:16:56.925
They are even inaccessible by car.

00:16:56.925 --> 00:16:57.806
It's a target on a moped.

00:16:58.387 --> 00:17:00.950
It can take 5 to 6 hours of walking to get there.

00:17:03.793 --> 00:17:04.314
In addition,

00:17:04.895 --> 00:17:06.296
You have to climb the mountain.

00:17:07.378 --> 00:17:09.760
It's sometimes very hard for someone like me to go there.

00:17:11.963 --> 00:17:14.945
The living conditions are really not comfortable for sleeping.

00:17:15.606 --> 00:17:16.847
The same applies to food,

00:17:17.528 --> 00:17:19.009
not to mention the hygiene conditions.

00:17:31.159 --> 00:17:32.660
What is all this wood you're transporting?

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.742
It was wood that was causing an obstruction at the foot of the dam.

00:17:36.082 --> 00:17:37.243
because of the floods.

00:17:38.364 --> 00:17:39.385
Are you using it to make a fire?

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:40.846
Yes,

00:17:41.967 --> 00:17:42.227
That's it.

00:17:42.488 --> 00:17:44.049
Only for making a fire.

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:46.851
And if we don't pick it up,

00:17:46.871 --> 00:17:47.572
What's going on?

00:17:47.573 --> 00:17:50.394
If we don't pick it up,

00:17:50.414 --> 00:17:51.895
This prevents water from flowing into the dam.

00:17:52.956 --> 00:17:53.376
Things are moving.

00:17:54.437 --> 00:17:55.938
And you're going in pairs to collect all that wood?

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:57.940
Yes,

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.281
We do this every day.

00:17:59.742 --> 00:18:00.362
Every day ?

00:18:02.344 --> 00:18:02.464
Yes,

00:18:03.344 --> 00:18:05.466
only during this period when there are heavy rains.

00:18:06.587 --> 00:18:07.268
As in previous years,

00:18:07.288 --> 00:18:08.128
We do this every year.

00:18:09.109 --> 00:18:10.090
Was it the same last year?

00:18:10.971 --> 00:18:11.431
Yes,

00:18:11.432 --> 00:18:11.531
Yes.

00:18:11.551 --> 00:18:11.991
Oh yes,

00:18:11.992 --> 00:18:12.592
It's always like that.

00:18:16.835 --> 00:18:19.557
Another dam has been destroyed by the storm.

00:18:19.878 --> 00:18:23.200
Lien is pleased to see that attitudes are changing,

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:27.524
since the farmers chose to recover the dead wood that was blocking the dam,

00:18:27.864 --> 00:18:30.286
rather than going to cut down trees in the forest.

00:18:36.271 --> 00:18:37.152
Traditionally,

00:18:37.512 --> 00:18:38.873
if the peasants cut down the wood,

00:18:39.353 --> 00:18:40.775
It's simply to make a fire.

00:18:41.055 --> 00:18:41.295
for the...

00:18:41.375 --> 00:18:41.735
kitchen.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.643
With the local officials she meets regularly in the field,

00:18:53.223 --> 00:18:57.486
Lien seeks to assess the human impact that can amplify the effects of the monsoon.

00:18:57.986 --> 00:18:58.967
The more we deforest,

00:18:59.367 --> 00:19:03.050
The faster the water flows, the more weakened the remaining trees become.

00:19:10.875 --> 00:19:20.680
The uncontrolled exploitation of forests destroys the balance of nature and the work of the Ienne consists of informing the villagers of the risks they are posing to the environment.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.862
Risks whose consequences are visible as soon as one ventures into the mountains.

00:19:28.944 --> 00:19:29.284
Before,

00:19:29.684 --> 00:19:30.605
There were trees.

00:19:31.145 --> 00:19:31.546
NOW,

00:19:31.926 --> 00:19:32.927
All the greats have disappeared.

00:19:35.629 --> 00:19:36.810
With landslides,

00:19:37.831 --> 00:19:39.573
the water can no longer drain properly.

00:19:41.034 --> 00:19:41.614
But then,

00:19:42.055 --> 00:19:42.555
The rice paddies have disappeared.

00:19:42.555 --> 00:19:44.916
those below are no longer supplied with water.

00:19:46.896 --> 00:19:47.336
Look at,

00:19:48.096 --> 00:19:51.617
Before, it was all covered in trees, and now there aren't many left.

00:19:53.518 --> 00:19:54.738
Every time it rains,

00:19:55.138 --> 00:19:58.799
Any area where there are no more trees is at risk of causing landslides.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.261
The earth collapses below and completely shifts the dam.

00:20:06.161 --> 00:20:10.943
There is also a lot of dead wood and branches that block the proper drainage of water.

00:20:11.943 --> 00:20:12.363
So that's good.

00:20:12.523 --> 00:20:17.291
if the inhabitants get rid of this wood and remove all the soil so that the water can flow normally.

00:20:27.967 --> 00:20:31.249
I was born and raised in a very mountainous region,

00:20:31.729 --> 00:20:32.909
where there were many trees.

00:20:35.591 --> 00:20:36.471
When I was a child,

00:20:37.011 --> 00:20:40.292
I spent my time riding and playing in the forest near my home.

00:20:41.293 --> 00:20:43.594
And that's also why I love my job so much.

00:20:47.211 --> 00:20:50.355
If Lienne is so sensitive to the problems caused by the monsoon,

00:20:50.876 --> 00:20:55.522
This is because his parents are also regularly confronted with climatic phenomena.

00:20:55.862 --> 00:20:57.384
When she visits her family,

00:20:57.825 --> 00:21:00.168
People always talk about the last flood.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.344
The biggest flood in the last ten years,

00:21:09.706 --> 00:21:10.446
I'm sure of it.

00:21:10.967 --> 00:21:12.509
It's really the same one as last year.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:14.171
That day,

00:21:15.292 --> 00:21:17.034
There wasn't any more of it all day.

00:21:18.336 --> 00:21:19.477
And it's late,

00:21:20.018 --> 00:21:20.859
late afternoon,

00:21:21.039 --> 00:21:22.040
around 7pm,

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.422
that's when it really began.

00:21:25.319 --> 00:21:28.901
We finished dinner and just as we were getting ready to go to bed,

00:21:29.662 --> 00:21:29.782
there,

00:21:30.062 --> 00:21:31.543
Everything happened so fast.

00:21:32.804 --> 00:21:33.224
Suddenly,

00:21:33.685 --> 00:21:35.006
The water began to rise,

00:21:35.386 --> 00:21:37.247
to climb at an incredible speed.

00:21:38.288 --> 00:21:38.448
Water,

00:21:38.908 --> 00:21:40.189
It reached above the knee.

00:21:40.189 --> 00:21:40.309
We.

00:21:41.369 --> 00:21:41.790
And then,

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:43.930
We had only one idea left,

00:21:44.631 --> 00:21:45.851
It's about seeking refuge elsewhere.

00:21:46.792 --> 00:21:47.212
We said to ourselves,

00:21:47.292 --> 00:21:48.252
Too bad about the furniture,

00:21:48.492 --> 00:21:49.413
We couldn't save them.

00:21:50.593 --> 00:21:51.313
There were plenty of them,

00:21:51.433 --> 00:21:53.474
full of objects floating all around us.

00:21:56.836 --> 00:21:58.636
Let's show each other how high it's gone.

00:22:01.998 --> 00:22:03.698
He had so much, or more, all day long.

00:22:04.058 --> 00:22:05.079
The water rose so fast.

00:22:05.579 --> 00:22:05.879
Listen,

00:22:06.099 --> 00:22:07.120
around 2 a.m.,

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:09.221
She had made it this far.

00:22:10.602 --> 00:22:11.142
Look at,

00:22:11.222 --> 00:22:11.723
That's crazy!

00:22:12.703 --> 00:22:13.584
Did you see the mark?

00:22:13.904 --> 00:22:15.245
You can see the difference in color.

00:22:20.908 --> 00:22:21.448
So what?

00:22:22.309 --> 00:22:23.409
Where did you put your things?

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:24.530
Where were they?

00:22:25.391 --> 00:22:25.611
Come,

00:22:25.691 --> 00:22:25.971
Follow me,

00:22:26.271 --> 00:22:26.871
I'll show you.

00:22:35.844 --> 00:22:36.985
I put them in the attic.

00:22:38.046 --> 00:22:39.106
Family affairs,

00:22:39.166 --> 00:22:40.007
like cushions,

00:22:40.127 --> 00:22:40.988
the covers,

00:22:41.008 --> 00:22:41.248
all of that,

00:22:41.348 --> 00:22:41.468
there.

00:22:41.668 --> 00:22:42.529
We put them up there.

00:22:54.397 --> 00:22:55.577
In his native village,

00:22:55.938 --> 00:22:57.679
Everyone knows about Lien's commitment.

00:22:58.059 --> 00:23:02.282
And the neighbors do not hesitate to ask her for help when it comes to planting.

00:23:04.531 --> 00:23:05.012
Oh Lien,

00:23:05.112 --> 00:23:05.832
