00:23:05.872 --> 00:23:06.913
Are you planting something?

00:23:07.414 --> 00:23:07.534
Yes,

00:23:07.734 --> 00:23:08.735
These are wind trees.

00:23:09.115 --> 00:23:10.116
Herbs against the wind?

00:23:10.496 --> 00:23:10.616
Yes,

00:23:10.716 --> 00:23:11.457
It's holding up well.

00:23:12.718 --> 00:23:13.519
Do you have any at home?

00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:15.380
No,

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:16.021
Not yet,

00:23:16.121 --> 00:23:17.542
But could you pass us a few?

00:23:19.003 --> 00:23:19.623
No problem,

00:23:19.624 --> 00:23:20.464
You just have to help yourself.

00:23:20.744 --> 00:23:21.565
Take several.

00:23:21.585 --> 00:23:22.466
We're going to plant them.

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:05.001
You see these plants,

00:24:05.502 --> 00:24:06.082
They are one year old.

00:24:07.204 --> 00:24:09.046
Now is the perfect time to plant them.

00:24:10.548 --> 00:24:12.069
A handful of soil and that's it.

00:24:16.872 --> 00:24:17.392
In your opinion,

00:24:17.953 --> 00:24:18.213
Tell me,

00:24:18.353 --> 00:24:20.095
How do you feel about the climate change?

00:24:22.637 --> 00:24:23.218
What we can say,

00:24:23.258 --> 00:24:24.158
that's because last year,

00:24:24.179 --> 00:24:26.481
There was a very severe flood.

00:24:29.864 --> 00:24:31.285
And this climate change,

00:24:31.405 --> 00:24:33.147
Do you think it's going to continue to deteriorate?

00:24:35.008 --> 00:24:35.128
Yes,

00:24:35.248 --> 00:24:35.869
I'm afraid of it.

00:24:38.872 --> 00:24:39.092
Already,

00:24:39.132 --> 00:24:41.354
We realize that the temperature is starting to rise.

00:24:42.575 --> 00:24:43.795
It's getting hotter and hotter.

00:24:43.796 --> 00:24:47.256
The climate is not reassuring and on top of that, so many trees have been cut down.

00:24:48.537 --> 00:24:51.577
Replanting is absolutely necessary to compensate for the negative effects of the climate.

00:24:52.318 --> 00:24:53.578
We really need to replant.

00:24:56.419 --> 00:25:03.040
Is planting trees only to combat flooding, or do you think there are other positive effects?

00:25:06.761 --> 00:25:09.662
I don't know, but when I plant a tree in the ground,

00:25:10.603 --> 00:25:11.523
That reassures me.

00:25:16.445 --> 00:25:23.808
Deforestation coupled with rising sea levels is causing a climate imbalance that is having a severe impact here.

00:25:24.008 --> 00:25:25.409
in the Kuan Bin region.

00:25:28.930 --> 00:25:29.770
On the coast,

00:25:30.031 --> 00:25:31.551
invaded by sand dunes,

00:25:31.851 --> 00:25:33.352
Desertification looms.

00:25:33.672 --> 00:25:34.292
Fortunately,

00:25:34.733 --> 00:25:36.253
young entrepreneurs like Mr.

00:25:36.753 --> 00:25:38.694
Vodainya are taking matters into their own hands.

00:25:42.136 --> 00:25:43.796
The climate has changed a lot here.

00:25:44.557 --> 00:25:45.377
When I arrived,

00:25:46.037 --> 00:25:47.058
It was very, very hot.

00:25:47.778 --> 00:25:48.258
The ground,

00:25:48.298 --> 00:25:48.919
the forests,

00:25:49.199 --> 00:25:50.919
the few trees that grew all around,

00:25:51.900 --> 00:25:53.581
Everything was there, but completely dried out.

00:25:53.781 --> 00:25:55.221
The sand was everywhere.

00:25:55.261 --> 00:25:56.942
It was like a desert here.

00:26:03.925 --> 00:26:04.825
Traditionally,

00:26:05.106 --> 00:26:07.026
plants that grow along the coastline,

00:26:07.166 --> 00:26:08.167
like mangroves,

00:26:08.427 --> 00:26:11.590
that one would normally find in these regions but which are disappearing,

00:26:12.050 --> 00:26:14.653
play a fundamental role in the protection of coastlines.

00:26:15.053 --> 00:26:16.194
They prevent erosion.

00:26:16.715 --> 00:26:17.735
They stabilize the dunes.

00:26:18.116 --> 00:26:19.217
slow down the floods.

00:26:19.637 --> 00:26:21.539
slow down the effects of cyclones.

00:26:21.779 --> 00:26:22.500
tide rats,

00:26:22.900 --> 00:26:24.922
and thus reduce climate warming.

00:26:37.195 --> 00:26:40.476
Mr. Vaudaïgnat is of the same generation as Lienne.

00:26:40.837 --> 00:26:49.800
And it is with the same conviction that he decided to change the appearance of the coastline by planting hundreds of thousands of trees on his property every year.

00:26:50.341 --> 00:26:50.701
For him,

00:26:51.161 --> 00:26:53.622
This is the best way to protect the Vietnam of tomorrow.

00:26:54.182 --> 00:26:57.724
He wants to open up Vietnam, particularly to ecotourism.

00:27:05.543 --> 00:27:10.767
The fuel shortage in the coastal region is so severe that most of the crops have been cut down.

00:27:11.187 --> 00:27:13.048
giving way to sand dunes.

00:27:21.554 --> 00:27:24.336
Apart from a few private initiatives like that of Mr.

00:27:24.737 --> 00:27:25.237
Vodania,

00:27:25.737 --> 00:27:33.603
Various international organizations have endeavored in recent decades to combat the formation of sand dunes by planting trees.

00:27:34.171 --> 00:27:36.238
But the attempts have often been unsuccessful.

00:27:36.600 --> 00:27:39.610
the young plants having been destroyed to make firewood.

00:28:05.735 --> 00:28:06.576
When I was young,

00:28:06.776 --> 00:28:09.360
I never would have imagined what my life would be like later.

00:28:12.383 --> 00:28:13.625
When I arrived at high school,

00:28:14.266 --> 00:28:17.109
I became aware of this through the news on television.

00:28:17.710 --> 00:28:18.531
with the newspapers,

00:28:19.132 --> 00:28:19.933
of all the problems.

00:28:20.073 --> 00:28:21.294
related to deforestation.

00:28:23.856 --> 00:28:27.498
Today I realize that there will always be work for me in this sector.

00:28:28.819 --> 00:28:30.000
Given everything that needs to be done.

00:28:35.704 --> 00:28:42.028
This work involves making villagers understand that trees play a vital role as a barrier against water.

00:28:42.589 --> 00:28:44.010
the winds and the sand.

00:28:49.143 --> 00:28:49.543
You know,

00:28:50.264 --> 00:28:51.304
What you need to understand here is

00:28:51.425 --> 00:28:53.606
It's because the people are very poor.

00:28:54.567 --> 00:28:56.068
If we don't take care of the fences,

00:28:56.908 --> 00:28:59.070
It's certain they will come to steal wood to make a fire.

00:29:01.011 --> 00:29:03.753
It is essential to put up barriers if we want to plant trees.

00:29:04.533 --> 00:29:05.134
Anyway,

00:29:05.614 --> 00:29:06.996
This is the only way to stop the dune.

00:29:07.496 --> 00:29:09.678
And then there's the sand piling up at the foot of the fences,

00:29:10.299 --> 00:29:12.461
It ends up creating an effective barrier against the wind.

00:29:14.583 --> 00:29:14.923
Look at,

00:29:15.724 --> 00:29:17.586
the beach was noticeably lower before.

00:29:17.926 --> 00:29:18.326
You see there,

00:29:18.607 --> 00:29:19.267
before this tree,

00:29:19.268 --> 00:29:20.529
It rose to 2.50 meters.

00:29:20.530 --> 00:29:20.949
And now,

00:29:21.129 --> 00:29:21.870
It's no higher than that.

00:29:33.711 --> 00:29:35.476
Encouraging farmers like Mr.

00:29:35.817 --> 00:29:38.665
Vaudaïna reinforces Lienne's conviction.

00:29:39.346 --> 00:29:39.808
For her,

00:29:40.088 --> 00:29:42.495
There is no such thing as fate, and there is still hope.

00:29:42.875 --> 00:29:43.596
A better world.

00:29:47.198 --> 00:29:48.839
I come from a poor family,

00:29:49.719 --> 00:29:53.061
but I was much luckier than others in being able to go to school.

00:29:53.861 --> 00:29:54.362
And now,

00:29:55.402 --> 00:30:02.206
It is my turn to give back what I have been given by helping people in difficulty and protecting their environment.

00:30:08.707 --> 00:30:10.189
This quest for a better world,

00:30:10.609 --> 00:30:12.030
That's also what Mr.

00:30:12.070 --> 00:30:14.292
Nguyen Thanh Hen and his family.

